# The Netlify subdomain serves the same build as the apex, and Netlify does NOT
# redirect it to the primary custom domain automatically — verified 2026-09-04,
# it returned 200. Without this rule quickiecoin.netlify.app is a byte-identical
# duplicate of quickiecoin.com. Kept first so a legacy path arriving on the
# subdomain reaches the apex in one hop rather than two.
#
# The `from` must be host-qualified: a path-only rule would match the apex too
# and redirect the site to itself.

https://quickiecoin.netlify.app/*   https://quickiecoin.com/:splat   301!

# Legacy paths from the v1 Nuxt site, which Google still has indexed and which
# return a Netlify 404 today. Each path below was confirmed to return 200 on
# https://quickiecoin.netlify.app before being listed here.
#
# The homepage is a single client-hydrated document with in-page sections, so
# legacy routes land on the matching anchor rather than a page of their own.
#
# Deliberately NOT a /* catch-all: that would serve the homepage with a 200 for
# every mistyped URL, turning real 404s into soft 404s. Unmatched paths fall
# through to 404.html with a real 404 status.

/locations/*   /#locations   301
/locations     /#locations   301
/faqs/*        /#faqs        301
/faqs          /#faqs        301
/wires/*       /#wires       301
/wires         /#wires       301
